{"id": "SL-f3c011", "title": "T029: Add Color field to CategoryCount domain and schema", "description": "Frontend expects category_counts[].color \(string\) for badge styling. Currently missing from both the domain CategoryCount struct and schema CategoryCountResponse.", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:00.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:00.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:response-shapes", "component:domain", "component:schema", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c010", "design": "1. In internal/domain/daily_action/daily_action.go line 174-179, add 'Color string `json:\\"color\\"`' to CategoryCount struct after Icon field. 2. In internal/schema/v1/daily_action.go line 78-83, add 'Color string `json:\\"color\\"`' to CategoryCountResponse struct after Icon field. Both changes are single-line additions.", "acceptance_criteria": "CategoryCount domain struct has Color string field with json:\\"color\\" tag. CategoryCountResponse schema struct has matching Color field. Both compile. Existing JSONB data without color field unmarshals cleanly \(Color defaults to empty string\)."}
{"id": "SL-f3c012", "title": "T030: Update mapper and briefing to include color", "description": "AgentBriefingToResponse mapper at internal/mapper/daily_action.go line 103-111 maps CategoryCounts but doesn't include the Color field. Also, briefing generation in service should produce color values for each category.", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:01.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:01.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:response-shapes", "component:mapper", "component:service", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c010", "blocked_by": ["SL-f3c011"], "design": "1. In internal/mapper/daily_action.go AgentBriefingToResponse\(\), add 'Color: c.Color' to the CategoryCountResponse mapping at line 109. 2. In internal/service/daily_action/briefing.go, update the briefing generation to include color for each category count. Use category metadata: replied=green, followup=orange, new_outreach=blue, meeting_prep=purple, enrichment=red.", "acceptance_criteria": "AgentBriefingToResponse maps Color field from domain to schema. Generated briefings include color values for each category. Response JSON includes non-empty color strings matching the metadata map."}
{"id": "SL-f3c013", "title": "T031: Add category metadata in GetDailyActions handler", "description": "Categories in the briefing response have empty icon, color, and description fields because the handler doesn't populate them. Frontend requires these for rendering category headers.", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:02.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:02.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:response-shapes", "component:handler", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c010", "design": "In internal/handler/v1/daily_action/handler.go GetDailyActions\(\) method, add a categoryMetadata map alongside the existing categoryLabels map \(line 231-237\). Map: replied -> {icon: \\"💬\\", color: \\"green\\", description: \\"Prospects who replied to your outreach\\"}, followup -> {icon: \\"⏰\\", color: \\"orange\\", description: \\"Follow-ups due based on your cadence\\"}, new_outreach -> {icon: \\"📤\\", color: \\"blue\\", description: \\"New contacts ready for first outreach\\"}, meeting_prep -> {icon: \\"📅\\", color: \\"purple\\", description: \\"Upcoming meetings needing preparation\\"}, enrichment -> {icon: \\"🔍\\", color: \\"red\\", description: \\"Contacts with missing data to enrich\\"}. Then at lines 255-262 where ActionCategoryResponse is built, set Icon, Color, Description from the metadata map.", "acceptance_criteria": "Each ActionCategoryResponse in the GET /daily-actions response includes non-empty icon \(emoji\), color \(string\), and description fields matching the category metadata table in data-model.md."}
{"id": "SL-f3c014", "title": "T032: Set generated_at and completion_rate in briefing response", "description": "generated_at is always null in the response even when generation is ready. completion_rate is always 0. Frontend needs both for display.", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:03.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:01:03.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:response-shapes", "component:handler", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c010", "design": "In internal/handler/v1/daily_action/handler.go GetDailyActions\(\) at lines 294-308: 1. Set GeneratedAt from gen.GeneratedAt \(already available on the generation domain model at domain line 22\). Add 'GeneratedAt: gen.GeneratedAt' to the DailyActionsBriefing struct literal. 2. Compute CompletionRate: if total > 0, completionRate = float64\(completed\) / float64\(total\). Add 'CompletionRate: completionRate' to the ActionProgressResponse struct literal at line 306.", "acceptance_criteria": "When generation_status is 'ready', generated_at is non-null ISO8601 timestamp in the response. completion_rate is a float between 0 and 1 reflecting completed/total ratio. When no actions exist, completion_rate is 0."}
{"id": "SL-f3c021", "title": "T033: Implement BuildPipelineSummary service method", "description": "Frontend expects pipeline_summary with 6 fields but backend never computes it. Need a new service method that queries contact and interaction data to build the summary.", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:02:00.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:02:00.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:pipeline-summary", "component:service", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c020", "design": "Add method to internal/service/daily_action/service.go: BuildPipelineSummary\(ctx context.Context, userID uuid.UUID\) \(*v1.PipelineSummaryResponse, error\). Implementation: \(1\) Query contact repo for active contacts by user -> total_active_contacts. \(2\) GROUP BY outreach_stage -> contacts_by_stage map[string]int. \(3\) GROUP BY lifecycle_stage -> contacts_by_lifecycle map[string]int. \(4\) Query interactions from last 7 days: count replies / count outgoing = response_rate_7d. \(5\) Count meetings booked in last 7 days -> meetings_booked_7d. \(6\) Avg time between outgoing message and first reply in last 7 days -> avg_response_time_hours. Use existing outreach repository and contact repository methods. If a query fails, use 0 as default rather than failing the whole summary.", "acceptance_criteria": "BuildPipelineSummary returns a populated PipelineSummaryResponse with all 6 fields. total_active_contacts counts non-deleted contacts. contacts_by_stage and contacts_by_lifecycle are maps with string keys and int values. 7-day metrics computed from interaction records. Returns gracefully with zeros if no data."}
{"id": "SL-f3c022", "title": "T034: Integrate pipeline_summary into GetDailyActions handler", "description": "Call BuildPipelineSummary from GetDailyActions handler and include result in the briefing response.", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:02:01.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:02:01.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:pipeline-summary", "component:handler", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c020", "blocked_by": ["SL-f3c021"], "design": "In internal/handler/v1/daily_action/handler.go GetDailyActions\(\) method, before building the final response \(line 294\): \(1\) Call h.service.BuildPipelineSummary\(ctx, userID\). \(2\) If error, log warning and continue with nil pipeline_summary \(non-critical\). \(3\) Add PipelineSummary field to the DailyActionsBriefing response struct literal at line 294.", "acceptance_criteria": "GET /daily-actions response includes non-null pipeline_summary when generation is ready. pipeline_summary contains all 6 fields matching PipelineSummaryResponse schema. If computation fails, response still returns successfully with null pipeline_summary."}
{"id": "SL-f3c031", "title": "T035: Rewrite Chat handler to Vercel AI SDK streaming protocol", "description": "Current Chat handler returns plain JSON {role, content}. Frontend useChat\(\) hook expects Vercel AI SDK data stream protocol with text/plain content type and code:json line format.", "status": "open", "priority": 1, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:03:00.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:03:00.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:chat-streaming", "story:US6", "component:handler", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c030", "design": "Rewrite internal/handler/v1/daily_action/handler.go Chat\(\) method \(lines 738-810\). New flow: \(1\) Parse request and extract userID \(keep existing lines 738-780\). \(2\) Set headers: Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8, X-Vercel-AI-Data-Stream: v1. \(3\) Use c.RequestCtx\(\).SetBodyStreamWriter\(func\(w *bufio.Writer\)\). \(4\) Inside stream writer: generate a messageId UUID. \(5\) Write start frame: fmt.Fprintf\(w, \\"f:{\\\\\\"messageId\\\\\\":\\\\\\"%s\\\\\\"}\\\\n\\", messageId\). \(6\) Call service.GenerateChatResponseStream\(ctx, userID, lastUserMsg, gen\) which should return a channel of string tokens. For initial implementation, call existing GenerateChatResponse\(\) and split the response into chunks to simulate streaming. \(7\) For each chunk: fmt.Fprintf\(w, \\"0:%s\\\\n\\", jsonMarshal\(chunk\)\) and w.Flush\(\). \(8\) Write finish: fmt.Fprintf\(w, \\"e:{\\\\\\"finishReason\\\\\\":\\\\\\"stop\\\\\\"}\\\\n\\"\) and fmt.Fprintf\(w, \\"d:{\\\\\\"finishReason\\\\\\":\\\\\\"stop\\\\\\",\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\":{\\\\\\"promptTokens\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\"completionTokens\\\\\\":0}}\\\\n\\"\). \(9\) Save assistant message to chat_messages. Reference: research.md Topic 2 for exact wire format.", "acceptance_criteria": "POST /chat returns Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8 and X-Vercel-AI-Data-Stream: v1 headers. Response body follows code:json\\\\n format. Starts with f: frame, streams 0: text chunks, ends with e: and d: frames. Frontend useChat\(\) hook renders streamed tokens correctly. Messages still saved to chat_messages table."}
{"id": "SL-f3c041", "title": "T036: Implement SSE Last-Event-ID replay", "description": "SSEStream handler reads the Last-Event-ID header on reconnect but doesn't query for missed events. Frontend EventSource expects missed events to be replayed.", "status": "open", "priority": 2, "issue_type": "task", "spec_context": "001-daily-bd-actions-api", "created_at": "2026-03-03T08:04:00.000000Z", "updated_at": "2026-03-03T08:04:00.000000Z", "labels": ["spec:001-daily-bd-actions-api", "phase:sse-replay", "story:US4", "component:handler", "version:v3"], "parentId": "SL-f3c040", "design": "In internal/handler/v1/daily_action/handler.go SSEStream\(\) method \(lines 460-519\), after registering with SSEManager \(line 483\) and inside the SetBodyStreamWriter callback \(line 485\): \(1\) Read Last-Event-ID header: lastEventID := c.Get\(\\"Last-Event-ID\\"\). Note: must read the header BEFORE entering SetBodyStreamWriter since c is not safe inside the callback. Pass it as a closure variable. \(2\) After writing retry:3000 \(line 491\), if lastEventID is non-empty: parse it as UUID, call h.sseEventRepo.FindByUserSince\(ctx, userID, parsedUUID\), iterate the returned events and write each as SSE: fmt.Fprintf\(w, \\"id: %s\\\\nevent: %s\\\\ndata: %s\\\\n\\\\n\\", event.ID, event.EventType, string\(event.Payload\)\), then w.Flush\(\). \(3\) If parse fails or repo returns error, log warning and continue without replay \(graceful degradation\). The SSEEventRepository.FindByUserSince\(\) method already exists and returns events created after the reference event's timestamp.", "acceptance_criteria": "When client reconnects with Last-Event-ID header, missed events are replayed in chronological order before live events. If Last-Event-ID is not a valid UUID or event not found, stream starts fresh without error. Events are replayed in the same SSE format \(id/event/data\). Live event loop continues after replay."}
